  data: {
    LLM: "Choose your Suit contracts early if you have a strong 6-card suit. Save the Nullo for when you have a hand full of 3s, 4s, and 5s. Never 'waste' a suit contract on a hand without at least one King or Ace. In Nullo, remember the Ace is your friendâ€”it's the lowest card (below the 3).\n\nManni Gambling: If your hand is 'almost' perfect for a Grand (e.g., 10 high cards), exchange your four lowest cards with the Manni. Even if you get worse cards, the risk is often worth it to secure a large point lead. Track which contracts your opponents have leftâ€”they may be forced into unfavorable situations.\n\nDefensive Teaming: Since it is 3 players, if the declarer chose 'Grand', the other two MUST cooperate to prevent them reaching 8 tricks. Lead suits that your partner is likely void in to force the declarer to use their high cards early. In Nullo, the declarer's target is only 4 tricksâ€”defenders should try to 'force' the declarer to win tricks by leading suits they must follow.",
    Player: "Choose your Suit contracts early if you have a strong 6-card suit. Save the Nullo for when you have a hand full of 3s, 4s, and 5s. Never 'waste' a suit contract on a hand without at least one King or Ace. In Nullo, remember the Ace is your friendâ€”it's the lowest card (below the 3).\n\nManni Gambling: If your hand is 'almost' perfect for a Grand (e.g., 10 high cards), exchange your four lowest cards with the Manni. Even if you get worse cards, the risk is often worth it to secure a large point lead. Track which contracts your opponents have leftâ€”they may be forced into unfavorable situations.\n\nDefensive Teaming: Since it is 3 players, if the declarer chose 'Grand', the other two MUST cooperate to prevent them reaching 8 tricks. Lead suits that your partner is likely void in to force the declarer to use their high cards early. In Nullo, the declarer's target is only 4 tricksâ€”defenders should try to 'force' the declarer to win tricks by leading suits they must follow.",
